  "body": "In https://github.com/w3c/html/issues/780 @travisleithead reported an security issue that affects `location.href` and `location.replace()`.\r\n\r\nWe could put the security restrictions @bzbarsky describes directly in https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#location-object-navigate or in the overall navigate algorithm. Not sure what is better/preferred? It sounds like at least in Gecko they are not merged with \"allowed to navigate\".\r\n\r\n(I think this does not affect the service worker `navigate()` API as you cannot get to that cross-origin.)\r\n\r\ncc @mikewest ",
